Z||000005||Steven||01-12-2000||05:31 PM||||The 84 Indy had a 4 cyl. with dual exhaust, so it could be done. It wouldn't have come from the factory that way, but still very doable.||||reg||3
Z||000006||batboy||01-12-2000||07:44 PM||||Actually Uaana, we had a whole topic about this subject already and the majority of us felt those vents should be left alone so the hot air can exit from them. BTW, I have an 87 SE with a 4 cylinder and it has factory dual quad exhaust tips. You just use the 6 cylinder tips, it all fits because the muffler is mounted in the exact same place.||||reg||1
